   *
   * This operation writes to the `discussion_board_settings` table. The Prisma
   * schema defines `key` as unique (@@unique([key])), `value` as string,
   * `description` as optional, `is_active` as boolean and temporal fields
   * `created_at` and `updated_at`. The server MUST enforce uniqueness on `key`
   * and return a 409 Conflict when violated. When the setting value is expected
   * to be structured (JSON) the API should optionally validate the JSON shape
   * based on the key semantics. Created records should set
   * created_at/updated_at; soft-delete is supported by deleted_at but creation
   * does not set deleted_at.
   *
   * Related operations and error handling:
   *
   * Use PUT /discussionBoard/moderator/settings/{settingKey} to update existing
   * settings. On failure due to validation (missing key/value) return 400 Bad
   * Request. On uniqueness violation return 409 Conflict. Authorization
   * failures return 403. Successful creation returns the persisted setting with
   * all relevant fields.
   *
   * @param connection
   * @param body Creation payload for a DiscussionBoard runtime configuration
   *   entry. Required fields: key (unique string), value (string). Optional
   *   fields: description, is_active.
   * @nestia Generated by Nestia - https://github.com/samchon/nestia
   */
